	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/mods_settings/prism_lighting/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Classic: the game's own light. PRISM Raster: each level lit by its light baked on this computer (bounced light, lamps and the sky, the sun's shadows sharp), with no ray tracing while you play."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="While Playing: a level's light is baked in the background as you play it, a quick draft first, then finished, picking up where it stopped. When Asked: only after Rebake Lightmaps."/>
		<string text="Max: the finest light and sharpest shadows, each texel baked until its noise is gone; slow, and large on disk. The others are quicker and smaller."/>
		<string text="Sky: the sky lights each place by how much of it the place sees, as in a path tracer: open ground fully, under cover less, a room with no sky only by what comes in. Flat: the game's own fill, the same everywhere. A change bakes again."/>
		<string text="Change this to bake the level you are playing again from nothing (needed after its geometry, materials or lights change; a finished bake is otherwise kept)."/>
		<string text='Shows "Baking lightmaps 37%" at the top left while a level is baked.'/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="PRISM Raster's brightness. Style's: Auto, which adapts as an eye does, a dark place staying darker than a bright one. Game's: the frame kept as bright as Classic's. Fixed: none."/>
		<string text="How light past white is drawn. Style's: Filmic, which rolls it off gently. ACES: punchier, a film's curve. Clipped: held at white, as Classic did."/>
		<string text="How characters, vehicles and weapons are lit. Baked Light: by the baked light where they are. Classic's: never darker than the game lit them."/>
		<string text="The sun's shadows of vehicles, characters and weapons. Traced: ray traced, on the ground, on each other and on themselves (a graphics card that traces rays). Classic's: the game's own, on the ground only."/>
		<string text="Draws the 3D view smaller and brings it to the screen's resolution, sharp and anti-aliased. FSR 3.1 is built in; DLSS is a plugin you build (docs/prism_plugin.md), used from the next start."/>
		<string text="What smooths PRISM Path Traced's light: PRISM's own filter, or DLSS Ray Reconstruction (a plugin you build, used from the next start), which also brings the view to the screen's resolution."/>
	</strings>
